From: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] luci-mod-network: hide Switch/VLAN config from the Network menu

The page stays reachable at /cgi-bin/luci/admin/network/switch-vlan: LuCI
only builds menu entries for nodes that carry a title, while the dispatcher
resolves routes from the entry itself, so dropping the title hides the item
without taking the page away.

---
diff --git a/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/luci/menu.d/luci-mod-network.json b/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/luci/menu.d/luci-mod-network.json
index 911a366..ad1e20c 100644
--- a/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/luci/menu.d/luci-mod-network.json
+++ b/modules/luci-mod-network/root/usr/share/luci/menu.d/luci-mod-network.json
@@ -47,7 +47,6 @@
 	},
 
 	"admin/network/switch-vlan": {
-		"title": "Switch/VLAN config",
 		"order": 12,
 		"action": {
 			"type": "view",
